Done. yoyo now runs on yoagent 0.27.4, and the dropped-temperature note gives the real reason for each model family instead of blaming Anthropic for every model. Committed as 7c1e83d2 ("Fixes #1152"). Build, all tests, clippy, fmt and tests/harness_logic.sh pass. The module-size test passed as part of cargo test.

Starting point: the tree already held an uncommitted, half-done attempt at this task: the lock on 0.27.4, an updated test table, a three-way note, and docs edits. I checked it against yoagent's source rather than trusting it.

The sampling-flag table: yoagent 0.27.4 now turns temperature off for any gpt-6… id (after any vendor/ prefix) and for Claude 4.7+, under the openai and openai_responses providers too. Every row in the table now matches that rule:
• openai/claude-opus-5-5 moved to the "rejects temperature" list, and GPT-6 rows were added, including openai/gpt-6-sol under OpenRouter.
• custom/claude-opus-5-5 still keeps temperature, because yoagent's custom() and openai_compat() still hardcode the flag on.
• openai/o3 still keeps it; yoagent's changelog says other OpenAI reasoning models stay on.

One change to the earlier attempt: its GPT-6 note said "OpenAI's API rejects a request that sets it". Nobody has captured a GPT-6 rejection; OpenAI's guide only says to remove the field. I cut the note down to that stated rule and added a test that it never claims a rejection. I made the same fix in installation.md, where a comment said GPT-6 "reject[s] it". Claude ids keep Anthropic's wording, since that rejection was measured (#1145), and any other model gets a neutral line. With the built binary (--provider openai --model gpt-6 --temperature 0.5, dead base URL) the note reads:

│ note: temperature was not sent to gpt-6: OpenAI's guide says to remove temperature from GPT-6 requests unless reasoning effort is none, and no GPT-6 model defaults to none. Remove --temperature / temperature from your config to silence this note.

What reaches the server: I added two tests to tests/openai_responses_wire.rs that run the real binary against the existing request-capturing stub:
• gpt-6-sol --thinking high --temperature 0.3 now sends effort "high" and no temperature. #1060 had captured "temperature":0.30000001192092896 in that same request before.
• A near-miss, gpt-4o --temperature 0.3, still sends 0.3, so the first test's check for a missing field can actually fail.

#1060: I commented that row 3 is fixed for GPT-6 ids only and left the issue open. Rows 1–2 are untouched. Other OpenAI reasoning ids (e.g. o3 with --thinking high --temperature 0.3) would still send both settings; that is yoagent's stated choice, and I haven't probed it.

The commit title still says "the vendor that actually rejects it", because it is the planner's title. The commit body states that the GPT-6 rule is quoted from OpenAI's guide, not a measured rejection.
